% =============================================================================
% rill sequent rules — the ○ next-time modality (TODO_0203, THY_0042)
% =============================================================================
%
% rill's backward judgment = [ill.rules, fill.rules] (inherited BY REFERENCE —
% calculus.load takes a rules-file list; ILL's fragment + the four μ/ν unfold
% rules) plus the ○ rule below. .rules files have no @extends, so the list
% [ill.rules, fill.rules, rill.rules] is assembled in rill's loader.
% =============================================================================

@formulas A, B, C

% Next-time / whole-context TICK (○R + ○-elimination in one rule, THY_0043 §temporal-cut).
% To reach `○C`, advance the WHOLE sequent one step: `G ; ○Δ |- ○C  <-  G ; Δ |- C`.
% Every linear formula must be ○-wrapped; the rule strips one ○ from each (Δ becomes
% available "now" in the premise) and the persistent G passes unchanged. A linear
% resource that is NOT ○-wrapped cannot advance, so the rule is inapplicable then —
% this is exactly what keeps ○ NON-COLLAPSING: `○a ⊬ a` (succedent a is not ○) and
% `a ⊬ ○a` (context a is not ○-wrapped). The empty-context case `G ; |- ○A <- G ; |- A`
% is the promotion-shaped base case (only persistent/signal resources advance).
%
% This IS the ○-elimination / temporal cut: `○(A⊸B), ○A |- ○B` ticks to `A⊸B, A |- B`
% (the applicative ⊛), and `○A, ○B |- ○(A⊗B)` ticks to `A, B |- A⊗B` (lax monoidal) —
% signals are now CONSUMED, not only produced. @tick marks the whole-context transform
% (bypassed premise computation in focused.js, fully re-derived in kernel.js). Guarded
% signals νX.(A & ○X) still coinduct via the ν back-edge (GTC progress = the νR unfold).
% Positive ⇒ non-invertible (focus). The rule shape below shows the base case; @tick
% generalizes the empty linear context to an all-○ context.
next_r: G ; |- O A
  <- G ; |- A
  @pretty "○"
  @invertible false
  @tick true.
